 folding fan as a dance prop.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic dance footage in a peaceful courtyard with pale stone paving, a wooden doorway, and softly blurred green bamboo. Gentle afternoon daylight illuminates the dancer's face and hands. The performance combines crisp fan movements with flowing arms and relaxed shoulders. Everything plays at natural speed, with no slow motion, frozen poses, or speed ramps.\n\n[Shot 1] The camera holds a steady waist-up medium shot at eye level, leaving generous space beside and above <Subject 1> for her arms and fan. She stands at a slight angle to the lens, matching the character in <Picture 1>. Her right hand holds a closed ivory folding fan by its pivot near her waist. Her left hand rests softly in front of her torso. She looks toward the fan with a calm, attentive expression.\n\nDuring the first three seconds, she raises the closed fan to chest height and opens it with one quick, controlled movement. The ribs spread into a clean semicircle with a soft snap. Keeping her fingers securely around the pivot, she sweeps the open fan across her chest from right to left. Her eyes follow its path, while her left arm extends outward in a gentle curve to balance the gesture.\n\nFrom three to seven seconds, she turns her shoulders smoothly into a three-quarter profile. Her right arm guides the fan outward and upward in one continuous arc, keeping it clear of her face. A subtle wrist rotation changes the fan from face-on to edge-on and back, revealing its thin ribs and lightly textured surface. Her left hand follows with a softer counterbalancing motion below shoulder height. Her hair and clothing respond naturally to the turn. The camera keeps the same waist-up framing, with both hands and the entire fan inside the image.\n\nDuring the final three seconds, she turns her shoulders back toward the camera and brings the open fan beside one cheek, slightly below eye level. Both eyes, her nose, and her mouth remain visible. Her left